{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself","id":1489560,"title":"A chronicle of someone going from the act of Awakening to Ascension itself","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-09T09:38:04-07:00","id":1489560,"title":"A chronicle of someone going from the act of Awakening to Ascension itself","content":"So I thought this might be interesting to the people here, <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/wija6e/i_played_a_mage_game_from_arete_1_to_ascension/\" target=\"_blank\">u/MistCongeniality is holding an AMA on reddit</a> about her experience of a whole campaign that took her from the earliest days of Awakening to actual ascending. There's also quite a few impressive incidents, including wiping out tremere chantries, encountering antedelluvians, romancing corax and taking over reality from Lilith.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here is a verbatim quote from the thread about what the experience was like for them, check out the thread for more details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So first \u201cIt was really interesting, and I want to preface this with:<br /> <br /> [Like Golconda, Ascension is in my opinion a personal thing that every ST will probably run differently and is best run as a collaboration between player and ST.My personal experience shouldn\u2019t be seen as me giving authoritative THIS IS ASCENSION prescriptions.]<br /> <br /> She hit arete 6 and I realized she was going to get there. She sat at 6 for a year real time, her longest arete. She hit arete 7, then very quickly 8, then I realized the characters story was finishing. So we had a short arc wrapping up some loose ends, then had a Final Seeking, which was hilarious considering my BB had only Harrowed up to this point. I ended up waking very very deep into the Horizon, past anything and everything I had even heard of before. There was a\u2026 boundary line? A division? And of course I\u2019m OOC crying at this point because this was IT and my ST was doing a <i>really good job</i> with the setting.<br /> <br /> And I ask if I can step over it.<br /> <br /> And he says, \u201ccan you?\u201d<br /> <br /> There were other mages nearby, frozen in reality, who couldn\u2019t or wouldn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> And that took some actual real thought and a silent table for a minute. Then, yes, she did cross. She gained access to a city-of-sorts that held all of the other ascended magi, including some jokes from earlier in the campaign (like Ea-Nasir). And then she met Lilith, the woman she had been obsessed with finding since apprenticeship, and she pushed her over this edge of folding into Reality and becoming One with it, like everyone else who lives(?) in that place.<br /> <br /> And the ST was so wrapped up in describing the transformation he forgot to ask about my ascension spell, but it\u2019s ok because part of what changed in the world as BB wrapped into it was what I was planning to cast anyways. So I just joked that since I shed thought forms at arete 7, she just cast without thinking. The plan was to give me one 10x10 spell to do whatever the fuck since that was end of campaign anyways.<br /> <br /> So uh short answer, it was jointing the cool kids club and becoming one with reality.\u201d<br /> <br /> Details: the final seeking was using thicker and thicker gangrel blood to eventually find Ennoia (and getting a free ice cream for meeting her 12th Antediluvian). She then used the sympathetic link, correspondence 7, prime 7 to cast a locator on Lilith. Then, since she had long eschewed the need to eat or sleep, she said goodbye to her family and her friends and began her walk.<br /> <br /> To me as player it felt like something she was compelled to do. BB never wanted Arete and only ever Harrowed, being dragged kicking and screaming into more magick. But this final thing was\u2026 correct? The final character moment of acceptance that she must die, but the peace of knowing this form of \u201cDeath\u201d is the correct one for her. The serenity of realizing she didn\u2019t need to pay a debt for her failure to die at the bomb site, that this is what her whole life was leading up to. The walk through the Horizon, while it had encounters, was mostly me narrating the thought processes of this character and how she\u2019d grown and changed through the years.<br /> <br /> Take all the notes you want and feel free to ask for more clarity, I know this is rambling but it\u2019s very hard to condense the climax of a four year campaign into a few paragraphs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I have no idea if I needed the prime on that locator. I used prime basically constantly because it couldn\u2019t hurt. ymmv on that kind of spell) </div> </div> </div>It might not be how I see Ascension, but it sure as hell sounds like an amazing experience and a highly successful chronicle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":".  Formatting 08-09-2022, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T20:27:55-07:00","id":1489603,"title":"","content":"The idea of Ascension seems very much connected with the Buddhist concept of Nirvana, and Buddism is sort of... Nihilistic. It preaches the dissolution of the Ego, to &quot;let go&quot; in order to remove oneself from the eternal cicle of reencarnation and suffering, which in buddism, suffering comes from attachment. The final path to achieve enlightment would therefore be to remove ALL attachments - which at end, would include attachments to the sense of the self.<br /> <br /> So, I get this idea of &quot;reaching death in the proper way&quot;, since this is what MtA pushes players towards inevitably.<br /> <br /> So, in this we get a few considerations... &quot;Ascension&quot; - or it's real life inspiration &quot;Nirvana&quot; - could mean the nihilistic ultimate dissolution. This is somewhat terrifying for us &quot;sleepers&quot;, because well, it just sounds like Oblivion. If that's the case, you must seriously begin to consider that hey, maybe the Nefandi are right after all.<br /> <br /> And I particularly like this view. This sets the tone for a TRUE horror game. This time however, instead of being personal horror, this is just and only Horror; ALL HOPE IS AN ILLUSION, THERE'S ONLY SUFFERING AND DARKNESS.<br /> <br /> Final &quot;Ascension&quot; is when you break the bounds of the prison of reality, to discover - to your horror - that there's only the eternal Void awaiting on the other side.<br /> <br /> That's a very macabre &quot;Cthulhu&quot; type of twist, upon which the entirety of the existance is just a sick joke, a prison designed only to torture its inhabitants in an endless cicle of torment, and in this one, the ones who know the truth are the Nefandi. And they could even be the heroes! Trying to put a definite stop to this senseless horror show.<br /> <br /> On the other hand thou, &quot;Ascension&quot; could be reaching a state of &quot;Oneness&quot; with the Divine or the Creation/Universe whatever. And... I personally dont see how could this be so much better. Because, at the end of the day, it revolves around the same idea of the dissolution of the Ego. You are no longer yourself, but instead you now are part of the &quot;universal hivemind&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lets say that, once you reach the Apex of Ascension, you're truly there, you become Omniscient. Alright? And when I say it, I mean it.<br /> <br /> So, now you basically have the same mind as &quot;God&quot;, let us put it this way.<br /> <br /> You know know as much as &quot;God&quot; do, you think as God do.<br /> <br /> In essence, you became &quot;God&quot; - or &quot;united&quot; with him.<br /> <br /> But so did all the others who reached that stage!<br /> <br /> In essence, you lose yourself... Whatever it is that made you, you... No longer exists. And it is now part of the &quot;universal hivemind&quot;. Sharing the same collective thoughts.<br /> <br /> In a way, you cease to be nevertheless. If you just becomes &quot;one with the universe&quot;, that also means you're... None.<br /> <br /> (or maybe Im an Arete 10 Nefandus recruiting new blood... But hey, regardless, I may be right...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T01:10:41-07:00","id":1489612,"title":"","content":"I think what Ascension actually is depends on the people running the game and what they perceive as Ascension. Their experiences and types of literature they indulge in will most likely shape what their Ascension will be like. There are many interpretations what it could be and if it relates to what religion and philosophy tell us, heck multiple things may be right for certain Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T08:28:39-07:00","id":1489636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489612#post1489612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what Ascension actually is depends on the people running the game and what they perceive as Ascension. Their experiences and types of literature they indulge in will most likely shape what their Ascension will be like. There are many interpretations what it could be and if it relates to what religion and philosophy tell us, heck multiple things may be right for certain Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like the idea of what I call as &quot;Techno-Ascension&quot;. The culmination of the transhumanist (dangerous) utopia. The best example would be the movie... Transcendence? Im not sure if that's really the title in english, but it's the one with Johnny Deep where he downloads his brain into a computer before death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T08:33:23-07:00","id":1489637,"title":"","content":"In my view, Ascension isn't something that most mages actively pursue; so \u201cwhat it is\u201d tends not to matter much. The only faction that actively promotes pursuing it is the Traditions; which means that \u201cwhat it is\u201d <i>also</i> tends to be viewed through their shared philosophy. That's why earlier editions pictured it as \u201cgrowing beyond your paradigm\u201d; because the Traditions as a whole espouse the belief that the differences in the magicks that each of them promotes are ultimately meaningless, and that as one approaches Ascension one will increasingly see through the illusions to the truth. <br /> <br /> But that's just the way the Traditions see it (and a handful of others, like the Batini and, ironically, the Hollow Ones). I would <i>not</i> expect the <i>Technocracy</i> to see it that way. Mind you, Technocrats generally aren't interested in Ascension; certainly not in the same way the Traditions are. When they <i>do</i> talk about it, they don't talk in individual terms, but rather in terms of <i>Mass Ascension</i>: bringing about a Utopian future for humanity as a whole. <br /> <br /> The Crafts, too, tend not to view Ascension in the same way as the Traditions. While they're more open to the idea of individuals Ascending, most of them don't buy into the Traditional concept of Paradigm and Practice as things to be overcome. Instead, their notions of Ascension tend more toward being the ultimate expressions of their Magickal beliefs. <br /> <br /> The Marauders take <i>that</i> notion to an individualistic <i>extreme</i>. If Magick is bending reality to your will, then it might be argued that the Marauders are on the truest path of Ascension. <br /> <br /> And Kakost neatly sums up the sorts of arguments that the Nephandi would put forward, about how the opposite of that philosophy \u2014 the <i>dissolution</i> of the self \u2014 might tend to be viewed by the average mage, for whom hubris is a close companion, as a horror. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, my own view is that Ascension is not something that can be understood until you get there. Just look at how radically one's worldview can change upon Awakening; Ascension is arguably just as radical of a change, and is likely to be incomprehensible to anyone who isn't at least almost there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T08:59:55-07:00","id":1489639,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it's something like Neo in the Matrix. All the humans on Zion are &quot;awaken&quot;. They lived in the illusion that were the Matrix, but a few of those just simply couldnt accept the program; deep down, those few individuals could feel in a subconcious level that something was off with the world.<br /> <br /> After &quot;awakening&quot;, those individuals were able to circumvent many of the limitations of the Matrix, allowing them to jump insanely high distances and other types of incredible feats.<br /> <br /> Neo however was &quot;The One&quot;. And he had a &quot;second awakening&quot;, which allowed to see the &quot;Deep Matrix&quot; in a way that went beyond and above of what any other could, basically gaining &quot;root access&quot; to the mainframe.<br /> <br /> Yes, Ascension would be an unthinkable - perhaps even unknowable - &quot;Second Awakening&quot;. Or, perhaps what mages refer to &quot;Awakening&quot; is just becoming &quot;sleep walking&quot;. And the &quot;true&quot; Awakening, when you TRULY becomes able to remove all the veils of reality, is Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T09:14:38-07:00","id":1489643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489636#post1489636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also like the idea of what I call as &amp;quot;Techno-Ascension&amp;quot;. The culmination of the transhumanist (dangerous) utopia. The best example would be the movie... Transcendence? Im not sure if that's really the title in english, but it's the one with Johnny Deep where he downloads his brain into a computer before death.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the extent that Technocrats <i>do</i> have a concept of personal Ascension, I tend to think that it looks an awful lot like Threat Null. Not <i>exactly</i> like that, mind you; but more like that than like any sort of Nirvana or joining the One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T12:45:30-07:00","id":1489665,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489637#post1489637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my view, Ascension isn't something that most mages actively pursue; so \u201cwhat it is\u201d tends not to matter much. The only faction that actively promotes pursuing it is the Traditions; which means that \u201cwhat it is\u201d <i>also</i> tends to be viewed through their shared philosophy. That's why earlier editions pictured it as \u201cgrowing beyond your paradigm\u201d; because the Traditions as a whole espouse the belief that the differences in the magicks that each of them promotes are ultimately meaningless, and that as one approaches Ascension one will increasingly see through the illusions to the truth.<br /> <br /> But that's just the way the Traditions see it (and a handful of others, like the Batini and, ironically, the Hollow Ones). I would <i>not</i> expect the <i>Technocracy</i> to see it that way. Mind you, Technocrats generally aren't interested in Ascension; certainly not in the same way the Traditions are. When they <i>do</i> talk about it, they don't talk in individual terms, but rather in terms of <i>Mass Ascension</i>: bringing about a Utopian future for humanity as a whole.<br /> <br /> The Crafts, too, tend not to view Ascension in the same way as the Traditions. While they're more open to the idea of individuals Ascending, most of them don't buy into the Traditional concept of Paradigm and Practice as things to be overcome. Instead, their notions of Ascension tend more toward being the ultimate expressions of their Magickal beliefs.<br /> <br /> The Marauders take <i>that</i> notion to an individualistic <i>extreme</i>. If Magick is bending reality to your will, then it might be argued that the Marauders are on the truest path of Ascension.<br /> <br /> And Kakost neatly sums up the sorts of arguments that the Nephandi would put forward, about how the opposite of that philosophy \u2014 the <i>dissolution</i> of the self \u2014 might tend to be viewed by the average mage, for whom hubris is a close companion, as a horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I so like everything you've said here. I'd also like to posit that most members of a Tradition are just like the Crafts, they are so focused on their paradigm and their foci that they don't really care about the Council as a whole. The way I read the Rev Tradbooks mostly leads me to believe that the majority of the Traditions are actually as hidebound and self absorbed as the Crafts, with only a subgroup being magickal ecumenicals into the Council spiel. And I think that's fine!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489637#post1489637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, my own view is that Ascension is not something that can be understood until you get there. Just look at how radically one's worldview can change upon Awakening; Ascension is arguably just as radical of a change, and is likely to be incomprehensible to anyone who isn't at least almost there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. That's why I noted in the beginning that I don't really see Ascension as the lady in the story and her ST did, but I fully support them making it their own story.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T13:48:32-07:00","id":1489673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489665#post1489665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I so like everything you've said here. I'd also like to posit that most members of a Tradition are just like the Crafts, they are so focused on their paradigm and their foci that they don't really care about the Council as a whole. The way I read the Rev Tradbooks mostly leads me to believe that the majority of the Traditions are actually as hidebound and self absorbed as the Crafts, with only a subgroup being magickal ecumenicals into the Council spiel. And I think that's fine!</div> </div> </div> </div>In that regard, it depends on how much you want to differentiate the Traditions and the Crafts. I prefer to emphasize the Traditions' cooperative nature, where the exclusionary mindset is most prominent in the lower levels but gets trained out of them by their mentors and peers as they advance, whereas the Crafts are practically <i>defined by</i> \u201cyou do things your way, and I'll do things my way\u201d \u2014 again, with the notable exceptions being the Ahl-i-Batin (who are all about Unity, and would <i>love</i> to turn the Disparate Alliance into Traditions 2.0) and the Hollow Ones (who take the \u201cit's all the same thing\u201d notion to a radical extreme, embracing the practice of Gutter Magic specifically to <i>avoid</i> developing a single \u201cHollower-approved style\u201d of Magick). And it's not a coincidence that they're the Crafts with the closest ties to the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T14:15:37-07:00","id":1489677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489673#post1489673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that regard, it depends on how much you want to differentiate the Traditions and the Crafts. I prefer to emphasize the Traditions' cooperative nature, where the exclusionary mindset is most prominent in the lower levels but gets trained out of them by their mentors and peers as they advance, whereas the Crafts are practically <i>defined by</i> \u201cyou do things your way, and I'll do things my way\u201d \u2014 again, with the notable exceptions being the Ahl-i-Batin (who are all about Unity, and would <i>love</i> to turn the Disparate Alliance into Traditions 2.0) and the Hollow Ones (who take the \u201cit's all the same thing\u201d notion to a radical extreme, embracing the practice of Gutter Magic specifically to <i>avoid</i> developing a single \u201cHollower-approved style\u201d of Magick). And it's not a coincidence that they're the Crafts with the closest ties to the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm usually running it as each tradition having &quot;leading masters&quot;, the people that tend to be the teachers and who average members of the Tradition flock to for tutelage and protection - Your average 3-4 dot mentors. These folks have their own views and preferences, and not all of them are that big on the Council stuff, they want to be left alone and do their stuff, and all this unity and all are one giberish just distracts them from it. So they end up ignoring it, or sending troublesome mentees over to the Council duties so they can master their own magic in the mean time. Others are huge proponents of the council and strongly encourage everyone to go to Council functions and socialise and trade ideas.<br /> <br /> It's of course something that's best ajdusted to the table that's playing it, but in general it seems to me that most Masters are stuck in certain patterns and fixations so badly that they miss the forest for the trees.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T14:45:41-07:00","id":1489682,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree about the \u201cI wish the Council would just leave us alone\u201d bit. But I see that as being distinct from promoting cooperation between the Traditions. In my preferred setting, the Council doesn't have much influence on the local level; but even so, there's a shared tradition that's developed over the centuries to promote ecumenical attitudes so that mages from different Traditions can and will work together and learn from each other \u2014 as opposed to the Disparate Alliance, where each Craft insists that its own ways are inviolate and where cross-Craft teams are rare and largely restricted to mutual defense. That is, the Traditions seek to understand each other, whereas the Disparates seek only to tolerate each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T15:00:36-07:00","id":1489685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489682#post1489682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is, the Traditions seek to understand each other, whereas the Disparates seek only to tolerate each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead magic, Book of Crafts and Lost Paths are some of my favourite sourcebooks for Mage.. As much as I like the Crafts having a prominent role, I'm just confused at their organisation and functioning. They picked the group of most hidebound, paranoid, standoffish factions in the setting and said &quot;Now Kiss&quot;. My pet theory is that it's a crazy working by the Batini to make a force to fight off the Nephandi threat, and that it's going to implode horribly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T15:25:54-07:00","id":1489686,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much the official line as well, with the addition of a hopeful \u201cbut you've got to start <i>somewhere</i>\u201d sentiment. Presumably, the intended story arc for the Disparate Alliance is for them to figure out how to work together, and become more than just an assemblage of insular Crafts. But for now, that <i>is</i> all that they are.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, though, that some are more insular than others. The Ngoma, for instance, wanted to join the Traditions. The only reason why they didn't was because the Order of Hermes kept on trying to stuff them into the Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we're drifting. My main point was that the traditions have that notion that all magic is different flavors of the same thing, which leads to those on the road to Ascension tending to generalize their views on Magick until they are all inclusive \u2014 or, in earlier editions of the game, discard their paradigms as distractions. Disparates, by contrast, lean into their existing magical views: they generally don't <i>care</i> if their own views on Magick can explain how other mages do their thing; so they seek to master their own style to the exclusion of all else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-10-2022, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T01:12:26-07:00","id":1489722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489685#post1489685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dead magic, Book of Crafts and Lost Paths are some of my favourite sourcebooks for Mage.. As much as I like the Crafts having a prominent role, I'm just confused at their organisation and functioning. They picked the group of most hidebound, paranoid, standoffish factions in the setting and said &amp;quot;Now Kiss&amp;quot;. My pet theory is that it's a crazy working by the Batini to make a force to fight off the Nephandi threat, and that it's going to implode horribly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe some of the Crafts could figure out what happened and why and counterbalance the Batini mistakes. <br /> <br /> I could see the Ngoma going to the Council and suggesting (with some force) that using African numerology and the number 16 might be a better choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T11:06:17-07:00","id":1489763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489685#post1489685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dead magic, Book of Crafts and Lost Paths are some of my favourite sourcebooks for Mage.. As much as I like the Crafts having a prominent role, I'm just confused at their organisation and functioning. They picked the group of most hidebound, paranoid, standoffish factions in the setting and said &amp;quot;Now Kiss&amp;quot;. My pet theory is that it's a crazy working by the Batini to make a force to fight off the Nephandi threat, and that it's going to implode horribly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Traditions did start like that. In fact, most Traditions were initially mortal enemies; one could say that the Ascension War is as old as Magik itself, the Order of Reason simply became better at it than all previous others.<br /> <br /> So, at the begin, the Traditions were set for mutual defense against a foe none could face alone, and they agreed to just tolerate each other - sometimes even agreeing to tolerate the intolerable.<br /> <br /> Some degree of trust and cooperation would only ever come with time, necessity and lots of shared blood and tears. You know, the type of brotherhood that only arise when you bleed togheter in the trenches.<br /> <br /> The same will probably happen with the Disparates, and in time they'll become the Traditions 2.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T11:10:41-07:00","id":1489764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489722#post1489722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe some of the Crafts could figure out what happened and why and counterbalance the Batini mistakes. <br /> <br /> I could see the Ngoma going to the Council and suggesting (with some force) that using African numerology and the number 16 might be a better choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, given time I believe that the Alliance will become a Traditions 2.0, and from that point onwards it really makes no sense for them not to formally join the Traditions into one &quot;The Great Alliance of Free Mages&quot; (or the &quot;Free Alliance&quot;, look I already have a cool name for it).<br /> <br /> The thing is, how much time for that (years? Decades? Centuries? Depending on the time needed, it could be too late)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T11:37:05-07:00","id":1489770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489643#post1489643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the extent that Technocrats <i>do</i> have a concept of personal Ascension, I tend to think that it looks an awful lot like Threat Null. Not <i>exactly</i> like that, mind you; but more like that than like any sort of Nirvana or joining the One.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's like the movie Transcendence - which by the way it is just Transhumanist propaganda.<br /> <br /> By the way, Transhumanism is the new Communism. As I'll always say, the Technocracy is a lot more like the Communist Manifest than Fascism (but then again, both are very similar, so there's that). So, technocratic &quot;Ascension&quot; is basically the totality of Transhumanistic ideas to their fullest - to me personally, that's more like another type of descent, and the stuff for dystopian nightmares. But that fits the Technocracy in my opinion, since the entire premisse of them is that they breed dystopian nightmares in search of their utopian goals (which is why they are the perfect representation of socialism and communism, the nightmare that is trying to achieve perfection).<br /> <br /> The Null Threat in a way is a twist on those transhumanist ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T12:31:30-07:00","id":1489778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489763#post1489763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Traditions did start like that. In fact, most Traditions were initially mortal enemies; one could say that the Ascension War is as old as Magik itself, the Order of Reason simply became better at it than all previous others.<br /> <br /> So, at the begin, the Traditions were set for mutual defense against a foe none could face alone, and they agreed to just tolerate each other - sometimes even agreeing to tolerate the intolerable.<br /> <br /> Some degree of trust and cooperation would only ever come with time, necessity and lots of shared blood and tears. You know, the type of brotherhood that only arise when you bleed togheter in the trenches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it. For someone who has been a singular society for over 500 years, they sure as hell do their best to keep their identity, practice and hubris to themselves and have a general preference for their own rather then some fair union of all. The Council is a dream, one perpetuated by people who are aware of the risks and who know they need protection and help along the way, but it's a dream many members perpetuating the core culture and identity of the Traditions pay only lip service to. I am all for the Council and see it as a core element of Mage, but the Traditions are not all in, if they were they would have long past the camps, the factions and the Tradtions themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T13:08:32-07:00","id":1489780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489778#post1489778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see it. For someone who has been a singular society for over 500 years, they sure as hell do their best to keep their identity, practice and hubris to themselves and have a general preference for their own rather then some fair union of all. The Council is a dream, one perpetuated by people who are aware of the risks and who know they need protection and help along the way, but it's a dream many members perpetuating the core culture and identity of the Traditions pay only lip service to. I am all for the Council and see it as a core element of Mage, but the Traditions are not all in, if they were they would have long past the camps, the factions and the Tradtions themselves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt mean that the Traditions managed to form a true brother/sisterhood of peers. Just that they achieved some amount of success (while accumulation a ton of failures).<br /> <br /> The only thing I was pointing is that the Traditions were like the crafts once upon a while. The only thing similar were the hermetic houses - which were the Traditions before the Traditions were cool. Before the Council however, you had Akashics and Chakravanti fighting, Verbena, Hermetics and Chorists fighting, and there wasnt even lip service to try to work togheter, it was more &quot;kill on sight&quot; diplomacy. Compared to that, all those segregationist crafts could be considered &quot;moderates&quot; compared to what the groups of misfits that were the ones that formed the Traditions. And what's worse, the Traditions were almost an Hermetic imposition upon the others, but yes, without the Hermetics it would never be, however their diplomatic skills werent exactly the best for the job; on the other hand, the Disparate Alliance have the guidance of the Ahl-I-Batin, who I believe have a much better chance of getting it to work than the hubristic hermetics. All in all, I do think that the Alliance have a good chance at becoming the Traditions 2.0 given time, and when that happens, the logical conclusion would be for the two groups to unite, since the Alliance will become too big to simply be ignored","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T16:11:33-07:00","id":1489805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489780#post1489780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Compared to that, all those segregationist crafts could be considered &quot;moderates&quot; compared to what the groups of misfits that were the ones that formed the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking about the same Disparate Council that consists of:<ul><li>Templars, who are all that's left of tha hardcore christian militant arm of the Technocracy who murdered everyone forever and still believe in purifying the world?</li> <li>Taftani, who still have a grudge against the Batini for excising their religion from their lands and enforcing Islam on their people?</li> <li>Solificati who no one trusts and belives they are just waiting to drop the next Heylel on them?</li> <li>Hollow Ones who are either bitchy assholes who brought up horizon because the cool kids wouldn't have them or a group that has no real organisation or structure to round up?</li> <li>Wu Lung who are essentially the Hermetics of China and Korea and believe they are the ones that have the Mandate of Heaven?</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T17:25:46-07:00","id":1489817,"title":"","content":"Technically, the Templar do not represent the remnants of the Cabal of Pure Thought. I will grant that they are home to the hardliners; but that's a relative term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T18:11:57-07:00","id":1489821,"title":"","content":"Some of those Crafts were <i>there</i>, they faced all the same problems that led the Traditions to put aside their differences or more, <i>and decided to be independant</i>. Of course, people change and some of them may be partial to make &quot;their own&quot; (with blackjack and hookers)...but...<br /> <br /> I fell it's not so much that it's unthinkable, as it's a thing with the execution. Perhaps it was too sudden, and not too well explored yet.<br /> <br /> My understanding it's that M20 tried to explain it by recycling the Revised ploy that was used to &quot;fold&quot; them into the Traditions: That they were too weakened by the Technocracy. Aint that it?- I don't like that plot point. Precisely in Revised, when the Technocracy and the Traditions are at their weakest, and declared a cease of the Pogrom/War, times are &quot;too dangerous&quot; for the Crafts to keep resisting like they did during the whole of the Ascencion War?.<br /> <br /> One can't really say &quot;it's the same as when the Traditions formed&quot;, because the Traditions<i> did form, </i>and that changes the history. One has to take into consideration that the Craft ate the whole of the Ascencion War alone, and proud of it, but precisely now times are changing for them more than they ever did before.<br /> <br /> It's not enough to say &quot;these things happen&quot;, sell/show us that it IS happening. Make it every bit as momentous as the Tradition's forming.<br /> <br /> Like, what did the Nephandi do - this time - that was so monumental it caused these factions to change?. The Technocracy blew up a chantry, and scared the fuck up of the greatest Seer ever, and then attacked the Council itself while fostering a brutal Inquisition, all of that helped quite a lot to join enemies together: That being so, what did it for the Disparate?. It HAS to be ... <i>cool</i>. I don't like if you can just gloss over it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what's worse, the Traditions were almost an Hermetic imposition upon the others, but yes, without the Hermetics it would never be, however their diplomatic skills werent exactly the best for the job; on the other hand, the Disparate Alliance have the guidance of the Ahl-I-Batin</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, the Order of Hermes originally didn't wanted to join. Hermetic do like to impose stuff, but this one was an imposition uppon *them*. Master La'Salle had to Duel so many Masters in <i>non-lethal </i>Certamen to build the oaths to *force* the Hermetics to join with the other sects, that he <i>died</i> ... Afterwards, of course they were dicks with everyone and bossed everyone arround. Which of course alienated many would-be members.<br /> <br /> The main diplomats of the old Council were the Ahl-I-Batin (well, perhaps below the Verbena) <i>, which it's also one of the main, if not the main, faction that founded the principle of Ascencion followed by the Council</i>. They grew disinchanted with that vision of Unity, but they were among it's authors<br /> <br /> The Ahl-I-Batin are the thing that, in my opinion, gives the most credence to any unity between these disparate factions on the Alliance, because they're experts at this and have done it before. But, as said, they also <i>failed </i>to recruit the current Disparate back then, when they had luminarias like Sh'zar the Seer giving credence to their plot. It would be nice to see how it's that they succeeded now.<br /> <hr /><br /> *Let's not make a Traditions 2.0<br /> <br /> I don't think we need Traditions 2.0. And I don't think the Alliance <i>needs </i>to be it in order to exist.<br /> <br /> This has been brought in these forums a lot, but it bears repeating: The Traditions have a very particular idea about &quot;unity&quot;, that of leaving aside your Focus, accepting a common magical lingo (the 9 Spheres), working in concert. Not everyone (perhaps not even a majority) <i>really </i>do all of this, but it's at least paid lip service. And at least the Systers of Hippolita explicitly refused to join because they rejected part of this meta-paradigm.<br /> <br /> This is not the only way to forge a unified faction. Even more, it's not the only idea about Unity, the Technocracy also has one of it's own<br /> <br /> So let's make a new faction with a different idea about Unity: Unity in diversity, explicitly eschewing a central power instead of trying to &quot;make&quot; one, allowing the members to rule themselves<br /> <br /> One thing that I really disliked about the Disparate was their legal system. Because their legal system forces members to be judged under the authority of at least two &quot;wise man&quot; of other Crafts ... and I don't buy it ... I can't see the fiercely independant Crafts just &quot;accepting&quot; a member it's going to be executed under the premises of a Paradigm not their own. I can't see them *not* closing files if they think the &quot;criminal&quot; doesn't deserve such punishment under their own law","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-11-2022, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T19:50:37-07:00","id":1489827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489821#post1489821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's make a new faction with a different idea about Unity: Unity in diversity, explicitly eschewing a central power instead of trying to &quot;make&quot; one, allowing the members to rule themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>This. If the Disparate Alliance is to be a thing, out should be this, rather than Traditions 2.0. Which means that I also agree with you about their justice system: if it's not consistent with \u201cUnity in diversity\u201d (a salad bowl rather than a melting pot), then it's BS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:51:14-07:00","id":1489844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489560-a-chronicle-of-someone-going-from-the-act-of-awakening-to-ascension-itself?p=1489821#post1489821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> 